  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Ballroom and concert dance music of nineteenth-century Vienna, developed from the 1820s by Joseph Lanner and Johann Strauss I with their dance orchestras and raised to its peak by Johann Strauss II, whose waltzes such as An der schönen blauen Donau (1867) and the Kaiser-Walzer (1889) were played alongside polkas and marches by the family orchestra with his brothers Josef and Eduard. The Vienna Philharmonic's New Year's Concert keeps the repertoire before a world audience. The generic strings and flute cards stand in for the dance orchestra's string section and flutes.",
